      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments): any comment provides a concrete real-world example (specific real-world case, instance, event, person, or documented situation) in support of its argument",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than OP). Return 1 if at least one comment provides a concrete real-world example, i.e. a specific actual case, instance, event, person, organization, statistic-bearing situation or personal real-life experience used to support its point. Return 0 if the list is valid and nonempty but no comment does so (purely abstract reasoning, hypotheticals, or generic claims). Hypothetical/invented scenarios do not count. Do not require external verification. Examples are nonexhaustive. Ignore the conversation column and any OP replies. Return 0 for a valid empty list; null if OC_comments is missing or malformed."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 56,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_uses_familiar_analogy",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments): any comment uses an analogy to a familiar scenario",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the JSON list in OC_comments (comments by users other than the OP). Return 1 if at least one comment draws an analogy, i.e. explicitly compares the issue under discussion to a different, familiar everyday or well-known scenario to illustrate or support its point (e.g. 'it's like...', 'imagine if...', 'consider a similar case of...'). The familiar scenario need not match any example here. Plain literal examples of the same issue, or mere topical mentions, are not analogies. Quoted text from others does not count unless the commenter adopts it. Return 0 if the list is valid and no comment does so. Return null if OC_comments is missing or malformed. Use current supplied text only."
    }
  }
]

